            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0379" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1949v01/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> S/S–NSC Files: Lot 63D351: NSC 52 Series</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Report to the National Security Council by the Executive
                        Secretary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Souers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-05">July 5, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"> NSC 52</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Governmental Programs in National Security and
                        International Affairs for the Fiscal Year</hi> 1951</p>
                <p>At a meeting in the White House on July 1, 1949, the President discussed the
                    budgetary outlook for the fiscal year 1951 with interested officials, including
                    all Council members, and presented the enclosed letter requesting the advice of
                    the National Security Council on the subject.</p>
                <p>Arrangements for the preparation of a draft response for Council consideration
                    prior to September 1, 1949, are being made with designated representatives of
                    the Secretaries of State, the Treasury, and Defense, the Chairman, National
                    Security Resources Board and the Economic Cooperation Administrator, in
                    appropriate consultation with the Director, Bureau of the Budget and the
                    Chairman, Council of Economic Advisers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sidney</hi> W. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Souers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d134-a1.xml" xpointer="d134-a1"/>
            </div>
